    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/bgsu/faculty/jobs/5521525/assistant-teaching-professor-btas-small-business-enterprise": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - BTAS-Small Business Enterprise",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor - BTAS-Small Business Enterprise Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Firelands (Huron), OH Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number BGSU02019 Division Fire-College Department Fire-Applied Science - Faculty Opening Date 10/19/2026 Description Benefits Summary The Department of Applied Sciences invites applications for a full-time, qualified-rank faculty, nine-month renewable appointment for an Assistant Teaching Professor with a broader skill set that includes accounting, marketing, analytics, and/or project management with a start date of August 2027. Information about Program and College The Bachelor of Technical and Applied Studies (BTAS) program at BGSU Firelands is seeking an instructor for their Small Business Enterprise concentration. It is a versatile degree designed to meet a growing job market. Students strengthen communication, critical thinking and professional skills while also increasing career-specific skills in Small Business Enterprise. BGSU Firelands was established in 1968 with the mission of making higher education accessible to students in Erie, Huron, and Ottawa counties. As one of Bowling Green State University’s seven undergraduate academic colleges and its sole regional campus in Huron, Ohio, BGSU Firelands is a driver of economic growth that is shaping the region’s future with degree programs that are accessible, affordable and in demand. With 2151 students, BGSU Firelands is home to a diverse group of undergraduate programs housed in three academic departments- Applied Sciences, Humanities, and Natural and Social Sciences. The Pathway program is offered at the Bowling Green campus. As a Public University for the Public Good , Bowling Green State University is a comprehensive, high research university located in northwestern Ohio committed to driving economic and cultural vitality in the region and beyond. Through innovative teaching, research and creative activities, BGSU fosters a collaborative and inclusive learning community where inspired ideas, knowledge and achievements support the region, state and nation. More than 760 talented and passionate faculty members teach across more than 200 undergraduate majors and programs, 17 doctoral programs, and 57 master’s programs. A focus on promoting research, scholarship, and creative activities has resulted in a significant increase in extramural funding over the past several years. Guided by Forward , BGSU’s strategic plan, the University is focused on redefining student success. For the fourth year in a row, The Wall Street Journal ranks BGSU as the No. 1 public university in the Midwest that students would choose again. BGSU also holds the Wall Street Journal distinction of being the No. 1 public university in Ohio for the student experience. Essential Functions Primary Responsibilities: Experience delivering and evaluating simulations related to business processes Develop curriculum related to small business needs at the undergraduate level Experience with the Canvas or similar learning management system Minimum Qualifications MBA or equivalent Online teaching experience 5 years of professional experience unrelated to higher education Experience teaching courses such as introduction to business, innovation in small business, sales in small business, public relations for small business, and applied experiences in small business settings Preferred Qualifications: Industry recognized credentials in project management, continuous improvement, human resources or other business-related areas. Additional Information Application Materials Required Cover letter Curriculum vitae Names and contact information of three professional references Insert additional materials required, if applicable for this search, which may include statement of teaching philosophy, evidence of teaching effectiveness, statement of research interests and agenda, digital portfolios, etc. Unofficial transcripts of highest degree earned are required for candidates invited for in-person interviews. Finalist will be required to submit official transcripts. BGSU policy requires finalist to authorize and pass a background check prior to receiving an offer of employment. Application Deadline The search committee will review applications until the position is filled; however, for best consideration, applications should be provided by January 8, 2027 . Salary & Benefits Competitive and commensurate with peer institution levels for rank and position in keeping with candidate’s experience and credentials. Full benefits package available. Expected Start Date : August 9, 2027 Bowling Green State University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to maintaining an employment and educational environment that is free from unlawful discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. The University prohibits discrimination and harassment on the basis of protected class: age (40 years of age or older), ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity and expression, genetic information, HIV/AIDS status, marital status, military status, national origin, political affiliation, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. EEOC Know Your Rights OCRC Know Your Rights In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Bowling Green State University, please call 419-372-8421 or email ohr@bgsu.edu . BGSU is an E-Verify employer. If hired into this position, you will be required to provide satisfactory proof of employment eligibility by providing acceptable, original forms of identification for employment verification via the Federal I-9 employment verification process. A list of acceptable documents can be seen here: https://www.uscis.gov/i-9-central/form-i-9-acceptable-documents Benefits Bowling Green State University provides a comprehensive benefit program as part of a total compensation package. This includes medical, prescription, dental, vision, health accounts (medical & dependent), life & disability insurance, retirement plans, employee assistance program and tuition fee waivers for employees and their eligible dependents as well as paid time off, flexible work options, holidays and parental leave. For more information, please visit Benefits-at-a-Glance . Employer Bowling Green State University Address 1851 N Research Drive Huntington Building Bowling Green, Ohio, 43403 Phone (419) 372-8421 Human Resources (419) 372-2865 Student Employment Website https://www.bgsu.edu/human-resources/careers.html Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/bgsu/faculty/jobs/5527776/associate-full-professor-director-for-school-of-built-environment": {
      "title": "Associate/Full Professor - Director for School of Built Environment",
      "description": "Associate/Full Professor - Director for School of Built Environment Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Main Campus (BG), OH Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number BGSU02063 Division College of Engineering and Innovation Department School of Built Environment - Faculty Opening Date 10/23/2026 Description Benefits Summary The College of Engineering and Innovation (CEI) at Bowling Green State University invites applications for the position of Director of the School of the Built Environment for appointment at the tenured Associate or Full Professor level. Given that the School comprises two growing departments – Architecture and Environmental Design, and Construction Management – the Director should recognize and value the distinct strengths of each discipline while continuing to cultivate collaboration and synergy across them . We seek a leader who strengthens our values of collegiality, trust, respect, and collaboration. The position has an expected start date of July 1, 2027. Information about the School, College, University, and Community School of the Built Environment The School of the Built Environment (SBE) capitalizes on the integration between architecture and construction management, where students in the two disciplines learn and collaborate, much as architects and construction managers do in their careers. The SBE offers undergraduate and graduate programs through two departments, the Department of Architecture and Environmental Design, and the Department of Construction Management, both housed in Kokosing Hall. The Master of Architecture program is accredited by the National Architectural Accrediting Board (NAAB), and the B.S. in Construction Management is accredited by the American Council for Construction Education (ACCE). The SBE has 16 full-time faculty and staff, complemented with professional adjunct instructors; they teach and mentor approximately 500 students. The SBE has experienced substantial enrollment growth during the last five years, more than doubling in size since 2022. The School Director would lead a distinctive school with accredited professional programs, conducive facilities, and strong industry connections. College of Engineering and Innovation The SBE is one of three schools in the College of Engineering and Innovation (CEI) , alongside the School of Aviation and the School of Engineering. Together they offer 21 undergraduate and graduate programs. The College has made experiential learning a pillar of its identity: the CEI’s nationally accredited cooperative education program has placed students with more than 5,000 companies since its founding. The new Technology Engineering Innovation Center adds collaborative labs and industry grade equipment to the College’s facilities. The College is also in a period of growth: the School of Aviation runs Ohio’s largest flight program through a partnership with the Bowling Green Flight Center and an airport on campus, and the School of Engineering, reconfigured in 2023, has added degrees in robotics, mechanical and manufacturing, and electronic and computer engineering. The College has developed a statement of vision, mission, and core values to guide its work. Its vision states that “The College aspires to lead by driving the societal, economic and environmental vitality of the region, the nation, and the world through creative and impactful engagement in teaching, experiential learning, scholarship and research.” Its mission reads: “The College cultivates a vibrant learning and scholarly environment founded on collaborative programs and industry partnerships that engage our students and our community in critical thinking, creative problem-solving and lifelong learning.” Six core values put that mission into practice: a student experience centered on success and career readiness; a collaborative community that recognizes and develops the strengths of its faculty and staff; multidisciplinary, accredited curricula strengthened by practical experience tied to industry and by cooperative education; fundamental and applied research conducted with students, industry, and the community; facilities that integrate emerging technologies to support teaching, workforce development, and research; and partnerships that prepare professionals and inspire the next generation of innovators. Bowling Green State University The CEI is part of Bowling Green State University (BGSU), a comprehensive, high research university in northwestern Ohio. As a “Public University for the Public Good,” BGSU is committed to driving economic and cultural vitality in the region and beyond. Through innovative teaching, research and creative activities, BGSU fosters a collaborative and inclusive learning community where inspired ideas, knowledge and achievements support the region, state and nation. More than 760 talented and passionate faculty members teach across more than 200 undergraduate majors and programs, 17 doctoral programs, and 57 master’s programs. A focus on promoting research, scholarship, and creative activities has resulted in a significant increase in extramural funding over the past several years. Guided by Forward , BGSU’s strategic plan, the University is focused on redefining student success. For the fifth year in a row, The Wall Street Journal ranks BGSU as the No. 1 public university in the Midwest that students would choose again. BGSU also holds the Wall Street Journal distinction of being the No. 1 public university in Ohio for the student experience. Bowling Green, the county seat and largest city of Wood County, is consistently ranked one of America’s best college towns. Its historic downtown is walkable and rich with local cafés and shops. Toledo is 30 minutes and Detroit is about an hour away, with Columbus and Cleveland within easy reach by car. Interstate 75 directly connects the city to both the Detroit and Toledo airports. Essential Functions The School Director is the chief academic and administrative officer of the SBE and reports to the Dean of CEI. The Director oversees the School’s programs, faculty, staff, and operations. S/he also represents the SBE to the University, industry, and profession. The Director leads the School in accreditation, program growth, faculty and student recruitment, fundraising and sponsored research, industry partnerships, and facilities, while advancing the vision, mission, and core values of the SBE and CEI. The duties and responsibilities of the director include to: Provide academic leadership for the faculty and staff of the School, fostering excellence in teaching, research and creative activity, and service to the University and community Implement the strategic plans of the University and the CEI within the School Build on the strengths of the two integrated departments Lead the School’s accreditation processes; i.e., maintaining NAAB accreditation for Architecture and ACCE accreditation for Construction Management; Lead student recruitment and retention across undergraduate and graduate programs in collaboration with University and College admissions and recruitment staff; Develop and sustain partnerships with industry and engage alumni as mentors, advisors, employers, and supporters of the School; Lead fundraising in collaboration with University Advancement, cultivating relationships with donors and sponsors, and to pursue sponsored research and other external funding while supporting faculty in securing grants and industry sponsorship; Lead the development of curricula and programs of instruction in collaboration with SBE faculty and the departments Supervise the graduate programs and develop new programs as needed; Oversee the recruitment, hiring, evaluation, tenure and promotion, reappointment, and dismissal of faculty and staff, and to organize the administrative structure of the School, assigning faculty and staff functions; and Serve as the fiscal officer of the School, allocating resources to the departments, monitoring operating and personnel budgets, and supervising the use of facilities, equipment, and supplies, including the development of laboratory and studio space. Minimum Qualifications A Master of Architecture (M.Arch.) degree or an equivalent terminal professional degree in architecture; or, a PhD degree in architecture, construction management, civil engineering, architectural engineering, or a related Architecture, Engineering, and Construction (AEC) field Outstanding teaching, research, and service credentials commensurate with the rank of tenured associate or full professor Experience in managing budgets Academic administrative experience Preferred qualifications: At least three years of distinguished professional experience in architecture, construction management, or a related field beyond academic work Demonstrated record of building a collaborative culture among faculty, staff, and students Proven record of effective leadership and administrative skills A demonstrated and outstanding working knowledge of architectural and/or construction management practices in the United States Registered as a licensed architect or Engineer in a US jurisdiction A passion and willingness to teach in an area of expertise, if necessary, and discuss pedagogical strategies Experience with leading NAAB or ACCE accreditation processes (or similar) Additional Information Application Materials Required Cover letter Statement of leadership philosophy with specific examples of the candidate’s work with faculty, staff, students, administration, and external partners Curriculum vitae Names and contact information of three professional references Recommended, but not required: a portfolio documenting professional experience Unofficial transcripts of the highest degree earned are required for candidates invited for in-person interviews. Finalist will be required to submit official transcripts. BGSU policy requires a finalist to authorize and pass a background check prior to receiving an offer of employment. Application Deadline Open until filled. Salary & Benefits Competitive and commensurate with candidate’s experience and credentials. Full benefits package available. Further Information Contact the Search Committee Co-Chairs: Ben Burghart, benburg@bgsu.edu ; and Yong Huang, yongh@bgsu.edu . You may also contact the School of the Built Environment at builtenvironment@bgsu.edu . Bowling Green State University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to maintaining an employment and educational environment that is free from unlawful discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. The University prohibits discrimination and harassment on the basis of protected class: age (40 years of age or older), ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity and expression, genetic information, HIV/AIDS status, marital status, military status, national origin, political affiliation, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. EEOC Know Your Rights OCRC Know Your Rights In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Bowling Green State University, please call 419-372-8421 or email ohr@bgsu.edu . BGSU is an E-Verify employer. If hired into this position, you will be required to provide satisfactory proof of employment eligibility by providing acceptable, original forms of identification for employment verification via the Federal I-9 employment verification process. A list of acceptable documents can be seen here: https://www.uscis.gov/i-9-central/form-i-9-acceptable-documents Benefits Bowling Green State University provides a comprehensive benefit program as part of a total compensation package. This includes medical, prescription, dental, vision, health accounts (medical & dependent), life & disability insurance, retirement plans, employee assistance program and tuition fee waivers for employees and their eligible dependents as well as paid time off, flexible work options, holidays and parental leave. For more information, please visit Benefits-at-a-Glance . Employer Bowling Green State University Address 1851 N Research Drive Huntington Building Bowling Green, Ohio, 43403 Phone (419) 372-8421 Human Resources (419) 372-2865 Student Employment Website https://www.bgsu.edu/human-resources/careers.html Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/bgsu/faculty/jobs/5530722/assistant-professor-ecology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Ecology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Ecology Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Main Campus (BG), OH Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number BGSU02065 Division A&S Dean Department Biological Science - Faculty Opening Date 10/27/2026 Description Benefits Summary The Department of Biological Sciences at Bowling Green State University invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position with a start date of 08/09/2027. This is a full-time, 9-month appointment for individuals with demonstrated research experience in Ecology, which may include research at different levels of biological organization. Information about Program and College The Department of Biological Sciences is an academic unit with 24 full-time active faculty, who conduct advanced research in a wide range of biological fields with significant impact on society ( https://www.bgsu.edu/arts-and-sciences/biological-sciences.html) . Annually, our program trains over 600 undergraduate majors and approximately 60 MS and PhD students. Our program emphasizes implementation of novel teaching and learning approaches and experiential learning through undergraduate research experiences and graduate research training. The Department of Biological Sciences is located within the College of Arts and Sciences. The vision for our college, aligned with the university’s strategic plan, is to ensure that our students graduate career-ready to meet the world’s challenges, and that our faculty research and creative activity contribute to the public good. We achieve this through robust collaboration across departmental boundaries, with particular attention given to increasing experiential learning for our undergraduate and graduate students and connecting our scholarly and creative work to the needs of our region. The College of Arts and Sciences is committed to faculty success, providing resources and support within the Dean’s Office and through collaboration with Arts and Sciences departments and schools, leadership teams in other colleges, and university-serving partners such as the Center for Faculty Excellence. Through these connections, we have developed a comprehensive, cohort-based mentorship program to support the professional growth and advancement of faculty across all disciplines and ranks. We value and practice shared governance and are committed to maintaining a vibrant and supportive working environment. As a Public University for the Public Good, Bowling Green State University is a comprehensive, high research university located in northwestern Ohio committed to driving economic and cultural vitality in the region and beyond. Through innovative teaching, research and creative activities, BGSU fosters a collaborative and inclusive learning community where inspired ideas, knowledge and achievements support the region, state and nation. More than 760 talented and passionate faculty members teach across more than 200 undergraduate majors and programs, 17 doctoral programs, and 57 master’s programs. A focus on promoting research, scholarship, and creative activities has resulted in a significant increase in extramural funding over the past several years. Guided by Forward , BGSU’s strategic plan, the University is focused on redefining student success. For the fifth year in a row, The Wall Street Journal ranks BGSU as the No. 1 public university in the Midwest that students would choose again. BGSU also holds the Wall Street Journal distinction of being the No. 1 public university in Ohio for the student experience. Essential Functions The successful applicant will be expected to maintain an active research program that results in publishing in peer-reviewed journals and obtaining external funding to support research. The successful applicant will additionally mentor undergraduate and graduate student researchers; teach undergraduate and graduate courses in ecology or related fields using traditional lecture and active learning pedagogies, and provide service to the department, college, and university, as well as to the profession. Minimum Qualifications • Doctoral degree in biology or a closely related discipline (e.g. ecology/evolution) by the start date • Primary research focuses on ecology, which could include research areas at any level of biological organization (from organisms, populations, communities to ecosystems and landscapes). • Demonstrated record of research productivity through at least three publications in peer-reviewed journals. • Experience teaching college-level biology as a teaching assistant or instructor of record. Preferred Qualifications • Experience implementing active learning pedagogies • Postdoctoral research experience • Experience seeking external funding • Experience in interdisciplinary collaboration Additional Information Application Materials Required 1. A cover letter including current affiliation and position, a short description of the reasons for applying for this position, and a short description of the candidate’s research focus/specialization 2. Curriculum vitae 3. A short description of the candidate’s Research Plan (maximum 3 pages) 4. Teaching Statement (maximum 2 pages) 5. Three (3) representative publications 6. Contact information of three (3) references that can provide a comprehensive evaluation of the applicant’s accomplishments and potential for success in their future research and teaching efforts Unofficial transcripts of highest degree earned are required for candidates invited for in-person interviews. Finalist will be required to submit official transcripts and letters of recommendation. BGSU policy requires finalist to authorize and pass a background check prior to receiving an offer of employment. Application Deadline The search committee will review applications until the position is filled; however, for best consideration, applications should be provided by January 11, 2027 Salary & Benefits Competitive and commensurate with candidate’s experience and credentials. Full benefits package available. Further Information For further information, please contact Dr. Juan L. Bouzat, Search Committee Chair: jbouzat@bgsu.edu Bowling Green State University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to maintaining an employment and educational environment that is free from unlawful discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. The University prohibits discrimination and harassment on the basis of protected class: age (40 years of age or older), ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity and expression, genetic information, HIV/AIDS status, marital status, military status, national origin, political affiliation, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. EEOC Know Your Rights OCRC Know Your Rights In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Bowling Green State University, please call 419-372-8421 or email ohr@bgsu.edu . BGSU is an E-Verify employer. If hired into this position, you will be required to provide satisfactory proof of employment eligibility by providing acceptable, original forms of identification for employment verification via the Federal I-9 employment verification process. A list of acceptable documents can be seen here: https://www.uscis.gov/i-9-central/form-i-9-acceptable-documents Benefits Bowling Green State University provides a comprehensive benefit program as part of a total compensation package. This includes medical, prescription, dental, vision, health accounts (medical & dependent), life & disability insurance, retirement plans, employee assistance program and tuition fee waivers for employees and their eligible dependents as well as paid time off, flexible work options, holidays and parental leave. For more information, please visit Benefits-at-a-Glance . Employer Bowling Green State University Address 1851 N Research Drive Huntington Building Bowling Green, Ohio, 43403 Phone (419) 372-8421 Human Resources (419) 372-2865 Student Employment Website https://www.bgsu.edu/human-resources/careers.html Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/bgsu/faculty/jobs/5530639/assistant-professor-molecular-biology": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Molecular Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Molecular Biology Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Main Campus (BG), OH Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number BGSU02066 Division A&S Dean Department Biological Science - Faculty Opening Date 10/27/2026 Description Benefits Summary The Department of Biological Sciences at Bowling Green State University invites applications for a tenure-track assistant professor position with a start date of 08/09/2027. This is a full-time, 9-month appointment for individuals with demonstrated research experience in Molecular Biology, which may include research at different levels of biological organization. Information about Program and College The Department of Biological Sciences is an academic unit with 24 full-time active faculty, who conduct advanced research in a wide range of biological fields with significant impact on society ( https://www.bgsu.edu/arts-and-sciences/biological-sciences.html) . Annually, our program trains over 600 undergraduate majors and approximately 60 MS and PhD students. Our program emphasizes implementation of novel teaching and learning approaches and experiential learning through undergraduate research experiences and graduate research training. The Department of Biological Sciences is located within the College of Arts and Sciences. The vision for our college, aligned with the university’s strategic plan, is to ensure that our students graduate career-ready to meet the world’s challenges, and that our faculty research and creative activity contribute to the public good. We achieve this through robust collaboration across departmental boundaries, with particular attention given to increasing experiential learning for our undergraduate and graduate students and connecting our scholarly and creative work to the needs of our region. The College of Arts and Sciences is committed to faculty success, providing resources and support within the Dean’s Office and through collaboration with Arts and Sciences departments and schools, leadership teams in other colleges, and university-serving partners such as the Center for Faculty Excellence. Through these connections, we have developed a comprehensive, cohort-based mentorship program to support the professional growth and advancement of faculty across all disciplines and ranks. We value and practice shared governance and are committed to maintaining a vibrant and supportive working environment. As a Public University for the Public Good, Bowling Green State University is a comprehensive, high research university located in northwestern Ohio committed to driving economic and cultural vitality in the region and beyond. Through innovative teaching, research and creative activities, BGSU fosters a collaborative and inclusive learning community where inspired ideas, knowledge and achievements support the region, state and nation. More than 760 talented and passionate faculty members teach across more than 200 undergraduate majors and programs, 17 doctoral programs, and 57 master’s programs. A focus on promoting research, scholarship, and creative activities has resulted in a significant increase in extramural funding over the past several years. Guided by Forward , BGSU’s strategic plan, the University is focused on redefining student success. For the fifth year in a row, The Wall Street Journal ranks BGSU as the No. 1 public university in the Midwest that students would choose again. BGSU also holds the Wall Street Journal distinction of being the No. 1 public university in Ohio for the student experience. Essential Functions The successful applicant will be expected to maintain an active research program that results in publishing in peer-reviewed journals and obtaining external funding to support research. The successful applicant will additionally mentor undergraduate and graduate student researchers; teach undergraduate and graduate courses in Molecular Biology or related fields using traditional lecture and active learning pedagogies, and provide service to the department, college, and university, as well as to the profession. Minimum Qualifications • Doctoral degree in biology or a closely related discipline (e.g., Molecular Biology, Microbiology, Neuroscience, or a related field) by the start date • Primary research focuses on Molecular Biology, Microbiology, Neuroscience, or a related area, with research that may span different levels of biological organization and employ molecular, cellular, genetic, biochemical, microbiological, or computational approaches • Demonstrated record of research productivity through at least three publications in peer-reviewed journals • Experience teaching college-level biology as a teaching assistant or instructor of record Preferred Qualifications • Experience implementing active learning pedagogies • Postdoctoral research experience • Experience seeking external funding • Experience in interdisciplinary collaboration Additional Information Application Materials Required 1. A cover letter including current affiliation and position, a short description of the reasons for applying for this position, and a short description of the candidate’s research focus/specialization 2. Curriculum vitae 3. A short description of the candidate’s Research Plan (maximum 3 pages) 4. Teaching Statement (maximum 2 pages) 5. Three (3) representative publications 6. Contact information of three (3) references that can provide a comprehensive evaluation of the applicant’s accomplishments and potential for success in their future research and teaching efforts Unofficial transcripts of highest degree earned are required for candidates invited for in-person interviews. Finalist will be required to submit official transcripts and letters of recommendation. BGSU policy requires finalist to authorize and pass a background check prior to receiving an offer of employment. Application Deadline The search committee will review applications until the position is filled; however, for best consideration, applications should be provided by January 11, 2027. Salary & Benefits Competitive and commensurate with candidate’s experience and credentials. Full benefits package available. Further Information For further information, please contact Dr. Vipaporn Phuntumart, Search Committee Chair: vphuntu@bgsu.edu Bowling Green State University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to maintaining an employment and educational environment that is free from unlawful discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. The University prohibits discrimination and harassment on the basis of protected class: age (40 years of age or older), ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity and expression, genetic information, HIV/AIDS status, marital status, military status, national origin, political affiliation, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. EEOC Know Your Rights OCRC Know Your Rights In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Bowling Green State University, please call 419-372-8421 or email ohr@bgsu.edu . BGSU is an E-Verify employer. If hired into this position, you will be required to provide satisfactory proof of employment eligibility by providing acceptable, original forms of identification for employment verification via the Federal I-9 employment verification process. A list of acceptable documents can be seen here: https://www.uscis.gov/i-9-central/form-i-9-acceptable-documents Benefits Bowling Green State University provides a comprehensive benefit program as part of a total compensation package. This includes medical, prescription, dental, vision, health accounts (medical & dependent), life & disability insurance, retirement plans, employee assistance program and tuition fee waivers for employees and their eligible dependents as well as paid time off, flexible work options, holidays and parental leave. For more information, please visit Benefits-at-a-Glance . Employer Bowling Green State University Address 1851 N Research Drive Huntington Building Bowling Green, Ohio, 43403 Phone (419) 372-8421 Human Resources (419) 372-2865 Student Employment Website https://www.bgsu.edu/human-resources/careers.html Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/bgsu/faculty/jobs/5530781/assistant-teaching-professor-biology": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Biology",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Biology Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Main Campus (BG), OH Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number BGSU02067 Division A&S Dean Department Biological Science - Faculty Opening Date 10/27/2026 Description Benefits Summary The Department of Biological Sciences at Bowling Green State University invites applications for a Qualified Rank Faculty (Assistant Teaching Professor) position with a start date of 08/09/2027. This is a full-time, 9-month academic appointment for individuals with demonstrated teaching experience in general biology education and microbiology. Information about Program and College The Department of Biological Sciences is an academic unit with 24 full-time active faculty, who conduct advanced research in a wide range of biological fields with significant impact on society ( https://www.bgsu.edu/arts-and-sciences/biological-sciences.html) . Annually, our program trains over 600 undergraduate majors and approximately 60 MS and PhD students. Our program emphasizes implementation of novel teaching and learning approaches and experiential learning through undergraduate research experiences and graduate research training. The Department of Biological Sciences is located within the College of Arts and Sciences. The vision for our college, aligned with the university’s strategic plan, is to ensure that our students graduate career-ready to meet the world’s challenges, and that our faculty research and creative activity contribute to the public good. We achieve this through robust collaboration across departmental boundaries, with particular attention given to increasing experiential learning for our undergraduate and graduate students and connecting our scholarly and creative work to the needs of our region. The College of Arts and Sciences is committed to faculty success, providing resources and support within the Dean’s Office and through collaboration with Arts and Sciences departments and schools, leadership teams in other colleges, and university-serving partners such as the Center for Faculty Excellence. Through these connections, we have developed a comprehensive, cohort-based mentorship program to support the professional growth and advancement of faculty across all disciplines and ranks. We value and practice shared governance and are committed to maintaining a vibrant and supportive working environment. As a Public University for the Public Good , Bowling Green State University is a comprehensive, high research university located in northwestern Ohio committed to driving economic and cultural vitality in the region and beyond. Through innovative teaching, research and creative activities, BGSU fosters a collaborative and inclusive learning community where inspired ideas, knowledge and achievements support the region, state and nation. More than 760 talented and passionate faculty members teach across more than 200 undergraduate majors and programs, 17 doctoral programs, and 57 master’s programs. A focus on promoting research, scholarship, and creative activities has resulted in a significant increase in extramural funding over the past several years. Guided by Forward , BGSU’s strategic plan, the University is focused on redefining student success. For the fifth year in a row, The Wall Street Journal ranks BGSU as the No. 1 public university in the Midwest that students would choose again. BGSU also holds the Wall Street Journal distinction of being the No. 1 public university in Ohio for the student experience. Essential Functions The primary responsibilities of the position are (1) to teach classes in introductory biology for majors and non-majors, and (2) classes in microbiology for health and nursing majors, which could include teaching and/or coordinating laboratory sections. Providing service to the department, college, or university is also expected. Minimum Qualifications • Master’s in Biological Sciences or related area (e.g., microbiology). • Two semesters of college-level teaching experience as a Teaching Assistant. • Demonstrated background (e.g., courses taken, teaching experience, research) in any biological discipline. Preferred Qualifications • Doctoral degree in Biological Sciences or related area (e.g., microbiology). • Two semesters of college-level teaching experience as an instructor of record. • Experience coordinating Teaching Assistants assigned to course labs or recitation sections. Additional Information Application Materials Required 1. Cover Letter detailing interest and experience in biology and/or microbiology 2. Curriculum vita 3. Statement of teaching philosophy and evidence of effective teaching success (e.g., student evaluations, classroom observation, syllabus) 4. Names and contact information of three (3) professional references. Unofficial transcripts of highest degree earned are required for candidates invited for in-person interviews. Finalist will be required to submit official transcripts and letters of recommendation. BGSU policy requires finalist to authorize and pass a background check prior to receiving an offer of employment. Application Deadline Position is open until filled, but for best consideration, please submit completed applications by January 11, 2027. Salary & Benefits Competitive and commensurate with candidate’s experience and credentials. Full benefits package available. Further Information Please direct questions about the application process to Dr. James Metcalf, Search Committee Chair, at jmetcal@bgsu.edu . Bowling Green State University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to maintaining an employment and educational environment that is free from unlawful discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. The University prohibits discrimination and harassment on the basis of protected class: age (40 years of age or older), ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity and expression, genetic information, HIV/AIDS status, marital status, military status, national origin, political affiliation, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. EEOC Know Your Rights OCRC Know Your Rights In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Bowling Green State University, please call 419-372-8421 or email ohr@bgsu.edu . BGSU is an E-Verify employer. If hired into this position, you will be required to provide satisfactory proof of employment eligibility by providing acceptable, original forms of identification for employment verification via the Federal I-9 employment verification process. A list of acceptable documents can be seen here: https://www.uscis.gov/i-9-central/form-i-9-acceptable-documents Benefits Bowling Green State University provides a comprehensive benefit program as part of a total compensation package. This includes medical, prescription, dental, vision, health accounts (medical & dependent), life & disability insurance, retirement plans, employee assistance program and tuition fee waivers for employees and their eligible dependents as well as paid time off, flexible work options, holidays and parental leave. For more information, please visit Benefits-at-a-Glance . Employer Bowling Green State University Address 1851 N Research Drive Huntington Building Bowling Green, Ohio, 43403 Phone (419) 372-8421 Human Resources (419) 372-2865 Student Employment Website https://www.bgsu.edu/human-resources/careers.html Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/bgsu/faculty/jobs/5530822/assistant-teaching-professor-fire-writing-and-english": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Fire-Writing and English",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Fire-Writing and English Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Firelands (Huron), OH Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number BGSU02022 Division Fire-College Department Fire-Humanities - Faculty Opening Date 10/27/2026 Description Benefits Summary The Department of Humanities at BGSU Firelands invites applications for a qualified-rank (a.k.a., non-tenure track) assistant teaching professor in writing and English in the Pathway program on the Bowling Green campus with a start date of August 2027. This is a full-time, non-tenure-track, renewable, 9-month faculty appointment. BGSU Firelands was established in 1968 with the mission of making higher education accessible to students in Erie, Huron, and Ottawa counties. As one of Bowling Green State University’s seven undergraduate academic colleges and its sole regional campus in Huron, Ohio, BGSU Firelands is a driver of economic growth that is shaping the region’s future with degree programs that are accessible, affordable and in demand. BGSU Firelands is home to a diverse group of undergraduate programs housed in three academic departments: Applied Sciences, Humanities, and Natural and Social Sciences. The Pathway program is offered at the Bowling Green campus. As a Public University for the Public Good , Bowling Green State University is a comprehensive, high research university located in northwestern Ohio committed to driving economic and cultural vitality in the region and beyond. Through innovative teaching, research and creative activities, BGSU fosters a collaborative and inclusive learning community where inspired ideas, knowledge and achievements support the region, state and nation. More than 760 talented and passionate faculty members teach across more than 200 undergraduate majors and programs, 17 doctoral programs, and 57 master’s programs. A focus on promoting research, scholarship, and creative activities has resulted in a significant increase in extramural funding over the past several years. Guided by Forward , BGSU’s strategic plan, the University is focused on redefining student success. For the sixth year in a row, The Wall Street Journal ranks BGSU as one of the Top 5 universities in the nation and the top university in Ohio that students would choose again. Essential Functions Teach 12 credit hours per semester in the areas of writing and English. Courses are primarily in person, but online and evening teaching may be required. Participate in professional development. Participate in department, college, and university service activities. Minimum Qualifications A master’s degree in English or a closely related discipline (e.g., rhetoric and composition) at the time of appointment Preferred Qualifications Experience teaching composition and writing courses and English courses at the undergraduate level, including as an appointed faculty member, part-time faculty member, and/or graduate student Experience teaching undergraduate students in courses and/or programs designed to assist with college readiness Additional Information Application Materials Required A cover letter that includes a summary of professional experience Curriculum vitae Statement of teaching philosophy Names and contact information of three professional references Unofficial transcripts of highest degree earned are required for candidates invited for in-person interviews. Finalist will be required to submit official transcripts. BGSU policy requires finalist to authorize and pass a background check before receiving an employment offer. Application Deadline The search committee will review applications until the position is filled; however, for best consideration, applications should be provided by January 8, 2027 Salary & Benefits Competitive and commensurate with candidate’s experience and credentials. Full benefits package available. Further Information For more information contact Matt Rome at mrome@bgsu.edu Bowling Green State University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to maintaining an employment and educational environment that is free from unlawful discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. The University prohibits discrimination and harassment on the basis of protected class: age (40 years of age or older), ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity and expression, genetic information, HIV/AIDS status, marital status, military status, national origin, political affiliation, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. EEOC Know Your Rights OCRC Know Your Rights In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Bowling Green State University, please call 419-372-8421 or email ohr@bgsu.edu . BGSU is an E-Verify employer. If hired into this position, you will be required to provide satisfactory proof of employment eligibility by providing acceptable, original forms of identification for employment verification via the Federal I-9 employment verification process. A list of acceptable documents can be seen here: https://www.uscis.gov/i-9-central/form-i-9-acceptable-documents Benefits Bowling Green State University provides a comprehensive benefit program as part of a total compensation package. This includes medical, prescription, dental, vision, health accounts (medical & dependent), life & disability insurance, retirement plans, employee assistance program and tuition fee waivers for employees and their eligible dependents as well as paid time off, flexible work options, holidays and parental leave. For more information, please visit Benefits-at-a-Glance . Employer Bowling Green State University Address 1851 N Research Drive Huntington Building Bowling Green, Ohio, 43403 Phone (419) 372-8421 Human Resources (419) 372-2865 Student Employment Website https://www.bgsu.edu/human-resources/careers.html Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/bgsu/faculty/jobs/5529095/assistant-teaching-professor-womens-gender-and-sexuality-studies": {
      "title": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Women's, Gender, and Sexuality Studies",
      "description": "Assistant Teaching Professor - Women's, Gender, and Sexuality Studies Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Main Campus (BG), OH Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number BGSU02068 Division A&S Dean Department School of Cultural & Critical - Faculty Opening Date 10/26/2026 Description Benefits Summary The School of Cultural and Critical Studies at Bowling Green State University invites applications for a Qualified Rank Faculty (QRF) Assistant Teaching Professor position (full-time, 9-month, renewable) in Women’s, Gender, and Sexuality Studies starting August 9, 2027. Information about Program and College The School of Cultural and Critical Studies (SCCS) includes four interdisciplinary programs with distinct but complementary missions: American Culture Studies, Ethnic Studies, Popular Culture, and Women’s Gender and Sexuality Studies. These programs share a multidisciplinary approach, eclectic methodologies, a commitment to critical thinking and engagement, and an emphasis on how differences—cultural, national, economic, racial, sexual—are constructed and expressed. For more information, visit our web site: https://www.bgsu.edu/arts-and-sciences/cultural-and-critical-studies.html The School of Cultural and Critical Studies is one of eighteen units within the College of Arts and Sciences. The vision for our College, aligned with the university’s strategic plan, is to ensure that our students graduate career-ready to meet the world’s challenges, and that our faculty research and creative activity contribute to the public good. We achieve this through robust collaboration across departmental boundaries, with particular attention given to increasing experiential learning for our undergraduate and graduate students and connecting our scholarly and creative work to the needs of our region. We are especially interested in recruiting candidates who can contribute excellence in teaching, scholarly/creative work, and/or service toward achieving excellence throughout the university and to the greater community. The College is committed to faculty success, providing resources and support within the Dean’s Office and through collaboration with Arts and Sciences departments and schools, leadership teams in other colleges, and university-serving partners such as the Center for Faculty Excellence. Through these connections, we have developed a comprehensive, cohort-based mentorship program to support the professional growth and advancement of faculty across all disciplines and ranks. We value and practice shared governance and are committed to maintaining a vibrant and supportive working environment. As a Public University for the Public Good , Bowling Green State University is a comprehensive, high research university located in northwestern Ohio committed to driving economic and cultural vitality in the region and beyond. Through innovative teaching, research and creative activities, BGSU fosters a collaborative and inclusive learning community where inspired ideas, knowledge and achievements support the region, state and nation. More than 760 talented and passionate faculty members teach across more than 200 undergraduate majors and programs, 17 doctoral programs, and 57 master’s programs. A focus on promoting research, scholarship, and creative activities has resulted in a significant increase in extramural funding over the past several years. Guided by Forward , BGSU’s strategic plan, the University is focused on redefining student success. For the fifth year in a row, The Wall Street Journal ranks BGSU as the No. 1 public university in the Midwest that students would choose again. BGSU also holds The Wall Street Journal distinction of being the No. 1 public university in Ohio for the student experience. Essential Functions • Teach a variety of undergraduate courses (4 courses per semester, mostly in-person) which must include introductory women’s studies and sexuality courses, and which may include other SCCS introductory courses in American culture studies, ethnic studies, and/or popular culture as needed within the school and in line with the candidate’s expertise. • Use inclusive pedagogies and/or a student-learning focused course design. • Provide service at the department, college, university, professional, and/or community level. Minimum Qualifications • Master’s degree in women’s studies or related fields (for example, American studies, cultural studies, ethnic studies, anthropology, history, sociology, etc.) required (currently or earned as of August 9, 2027). • Demonstrated record in research/scholarly accomplishments (e.g., academic publication—book, book chapter, journal article; academic paper presentation). • Demonstrated record of undergraduate teaching effectiveness (e.g., positive feedback from students, peers, or supervisors on instructional activities, performance as a teaching assistant, performance as instructor of record). Preferred Qualifications • Ph.D. in women’s studies, cultural studies, American studies, or related field of humanities and social sciences. • Institutional, professional, and/or community-level service experience. Additional Information Application Materials Required - Cover letter, detailing position-related teaching experience and teaching philosophy, and outlining research/scholarship accomplishments relevant to this position. - Curriculum vitae. - Sample course syllabus and assignment. - Names and contact information of three professional references. Unofficial transcripts of highest degree earned are required for candidates invited for in-person interviews. Finalists will be required to submit official transcripts. BGSU policy requires finalists to authorize and pass a background check prior to receiving an offer of employment. Application Deadline The search committee will review applications until the position is filled; however, for best consideration, applications should be provided by November 25, 2026. Salary & Benefits Competitive and commensurate with candidate’s experience and credentials. Full benefits package available. Further Information Dr. Tom Edge ( tjedge@bgsu.edu ), Search Committee Chair. Bowling Green State University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to maintaining an employment and educational environment that is free from unlawful discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. The University prohibits discrimination and harassment on the basis of protected class: age (40 years of age or older), ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity and expression, genetic information, HIV/AIDS status, marital status, military status, national origin, political affiliation, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. EEOC Know Your Rights OCRC Know Your Rights In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Bowling Green State University, please call 419-372-8421 or email ohr@bgsu.edu . BGSU is an E-Verify employer. If hired into this position, you will be required to provide satisfactory proof of employment eligibility by providing acceptable, original forms of identification for employment verification via the Federal I-9 employment verification process. A list of acceptable documents can be seen here: https://www.uscis.gov/i-9-central/form-i-9-acceptable-documents Benefits Bowling Green State University provides a comprehensive benefit program as part of a total compensation package. This includes medical, prescription, dental, vision, health accounts (medical & dependent), life & disability insurance, retirement plans, employee assistance program and tuition fee waivers for employees and their eligible dependents as well as paid time off, flexible work options, holidays and parental leave. For more information, please visit Benefits-at-a-Glance . Employer Bowling Green State University Address 1851 N Research Drive Huntington Building Bowling Green, Ohio, 43403 Phone (419) 372-8421 Human Resources (419) 372-2865 Student Employment Website https://www.bgsu.edu/human-resources/careers.html Apply"
    },
    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/bgsu/faculty/jobs/5532351/director-of-orchestral-activities-open-rank": {
      "title": "Director of Orchestral Activities (Open Rank)",
      "description": "Director of Orchestral Activities (Open Rank) Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Main Campus (BG), OH Job Type Full-Time Faculty Job Number BGSU02072 Division Musical Arts Dean Department Music Performance Studies - Faculty Opening Date 10/28/2026 Description Benefits Summary The Department of Music Performance Studies at Bowling Green State University’s College of Musical Arts invites applications for Director of Orchestral Activities, open rank depending upon qualifications and experience of successful candidate. Tenure-track, 9-month appointment, beginning August 2027. Information about Program and College Bowling Green State University’s College of Musical Arts has earned a reputation as one of the country’s outstanding collegiate music programs. The College enrolls approximately 475 students under the guidance of 55 full-time and 30 part-time faculty. Our comprehensive music curriculum features specialties in music education and contemporary music, including the distinctive DMA in Contemporary Music. The College is home to the MidAmerican Center for Contemporary Music, producing an annual New Music Festival and a nationally syndicated radio program. The College’s musical calendar features more than 300 performances and presentations annually by faculty, world renown guest artists, and 30+ student ensembles. Additional information is found at the College of Musical Arts website. The Director of Orchestral Studies conducts the BG Philharmonia and serves as Music Director for BGSU Opera Theatre productions. Other duties include teaching undergraduate and graduate conducting courses, mentoring orchestral conducting graduate students at the master’s and doctoral levels, and participation in college-level recruitment activities. Work collaboratively with the Director of Bands, Choral Activities, Jazz Activities, and Coordinator of Opera in facilitating the artistic vision and administrative operations of the large ensembles of the College. A full-sized symphonic orchestra, the BG Philharmonia performs three concerts per semester, one fully staged opera per year, and presents occasional special events and concerts on campus and throughout the region. Celebrating its centenary in 2018-2019, the BG Philharmonia maintains a storied history and legacy and will continue to honor traditions while embracing innovation into the next century. As a Public University for the Public Good , Bowling Green State University is a comprehensive, high research university located in northwestern Ohio committed to driving economic and cultural vitality in the region and beyond. Through innovative teaching, research and creative activities, BGSU fosters a collaborative and inclusive learning community where inspired ideas, knowledge and achievements support the region, state and nation. More than 760 talented and passionate faculty members teach across more than 200 undergraduate majors and programs, 17 doctoral programs, and 57 master’s programs. A focus on promoting research, scholarship, and creative activities has resulted in a significant increase in extramural funding over the past several years. Guided by Forward , BGSU’s strategic plan, the University is focused on redefining student success. For the fifth year in a row, The Wall Street Journal ranks BGSU as the No. 1 public university in the Midwest that students would choose again. BGSU also holds the Wall Street Journal distinction of being the No. 1 public university in Ohio for the student experience. Essential Functions Serve as Director of Orchestral Activities, guiding all aspects of the orchestral program at BGSU, and work collaboratively with the Director of Bands, Choral Activities, Jazz Activities, and Coordinator of Opera in facilitating the artistic vision and administrative operations of the large ensembles of the College. Teaching responsibilities include director of the BG Philharmonia, undergraduate and graduate conducting and literature courses, advising of graduate research and conducting projects, and other duties as assigned. Develop and maintain successful associations with local, regional, and national orchestral communities and schools, through visits, workshops, and guest conducting appearances. Actively participate in regional and national recruitment of highly qualified undergraduate and graduate students. Establish and maintain a national artistic profile in orchestral conducting, research, and creative activity within the profession. Contribute to institutional and professional service and the artistic and intellectual life of the College and University. Minimum Qualifications Master of Music (MM) required Minimum 3 years conducting orchestral ensembles at the collegiate level as instructor of record or professional orchestral conducting experience. Preferred Qualifications Doctor of Musical Arts (DMA) or Doctor of Philosophy in Conducting (PhD) 5 years of collegiate teaching experience. Additional Information Application Materials Required Cover letter indicating interest in and qualifications for the position Curriculum vitae Unofficial transcript of the highest degree attained Three to five references including names and complete contact information List of online or YouTube links to audio/video recordings of recent conducting performances (within the last three years) Unofficial transcripts of highest degree earned are required for candidates invited for in-person interviews. Finalist will be required to submit official transcripts. BGSU policy requires finalist to authorize and pass a background check prior to receiving an offer of employment. Application Deadline The search committee will review applications until the position is filled; however, for best consideration, applications should be provided by November 30, 2026 . Salary & Benefits Competitive and commensurate with peer institution levels for rank and position in keeping with candidate’s experience and credentials. Full benefits package available. Further Information: Questions concerning the search may be directed to Dr. Brian Snow, Director of Orchestral Activities search committee chair ( besnow@bgsu.edu ) You may also visit the college website at www.bgsu.edu/music. Bowling Green State University is an equal opportunity employer. The University is committed to maintaining an employment and educational environment that is free from unlawful discrimination, harassment, and retaliation. The University prohibits discrimination and harassment on the basis of protected class: age (40 years of age or older), ancestry, color, disability, ethnicity, familial status, gender, gender identity and expression, genetic information, HIV/AIDS status, marital status, military status, national origin, political affiliation, pregnancy, race, religion, sex, sexual orientation, protected veteran status, or any other legally protected characteristic. EEOC Know Your Rights OCRC Know Your Rights In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADAAA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Bowling Green State University, please call 419-372-8421 or email ohr@bgsu.edu . BGSU is an E-Verify employer. If hired into this position, you will be required to provide satisfactory proof of employment eligibility by providing acceptable, original forms of identification for employment verification via the Federal I-9 employment verification process. A list of acceptable documents can be seen here: https://www.uscis.gov/i-9-central/form-i-9-acceptable-documents Benefits Bowling Green State University provides a comprehensive benefit program as part of a total compensation package. This includes medical, prescription, dental, vision, health accounts (medical & dependent), life & disability insurance, retirement plans, employee assistance program and tuition fee waivers for employees and their eligible dependents as well as paid time off, flexible work options, holidays and parental leave. For more information, please visit Benefits-at-a-Glance . Employer Bowling Green State University Address 1851 N Research Drive Huntington Building Bowling Green, Ohio, 43403 Phone (419) 372-8421 Human Resources (419) 372-2865 Student Employment Website https://www.bgsu.edu/human-resources/careers.html Apply"
    }
